## The spec template itself

Every mechanism doc should use one rigid template:

```text
# Mechanism: POLICY COMMIT / REVEAL

## Purpose
Why the mechanism exists.

## Canonical status
GAMEPLAY / ANALYTICS / NARRATIVE

## Inputs
Exact input objects.

## State
Persistent and ephemeral state.

## Transition
Formal sequence.

## Outputs
Objects/events emitted.

## Invariants
Things that can never be violated.

## Information visibility
Who can see what and when.

## Determinism
How RNG/time is handled.

## Failure modes
Timeout, invalid action, corrupted state, etc.

## Edge cases
Tie, double KO, disconnected policy...

## Telemetry
Metrics emitted.

## Versioning
What increments version.

## Security
Sandbox implications.

## Tests
Required unit/property/fuzz tests.

## Examples
At least one normal and one adversarial example.

## Non-goals
What this mechanism does NOT establish.
```

That forces out ambiguity.

